# ── Single Cloudflare Pages project · 4 sites in one deploy ───────────────────
# One project (digimax) serves all four DSM webs because the Cloudflare account
# is at its 100/100 Pages-project cap — see CONSOLIDATION.md. Each site is a
# self-contained bundle under its own path; real files serve directly, and each
# path gets its own SPA fallback so client-side routing works per-site.

# ── DSM AI Labs rebrand: subdomains on the SAME digimax deployment ────────────
# marketing / agentic / creatives / admin .digitalsoftwaremarket.ai are all
# attached as extra custom domains on this one Pages project (still just one
# build, one deploy — no new project, same 100/100 cap constraint). Cloudflare
# Pages matches these rules against the request's Host header, so they only
# fire for that exact subdomain; the root domain, beta.*, and the *.pages.dev
# URL fall through untouched to the rules below.
#
# Rule order matters: the "already-prefixed" passthrough for each site must
# come before that site's catch-all, so a request that already carries the
# real path (e.g. an absolute /admin/assets/... asset request) isn't
# double-prefixed by the catch-all underneath it.

# Admin — admin.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai. admin-app's own asset refs are
# absolute (/admin/...), so those already resolve directly against the shared
# deployment; only bare/deep paths need falling back to the app shell.
https://admin.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai/admin/*        /admin/:splat            200
https://admin.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai/*              /admin/index.html        200

# Marketing — marketing.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai. public/marketing assets are
# also absolute-path (/marketing/...), so a transparent 200 rewrite keeps a
# clean root URL on the subdomain with no visible redirect hop.
https://marketing.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai/marketing/*  /marketing/:splat      200
https://marketing.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai/*            /marketing/index.html  200

# Agentic / AI services — agentic.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai. dsmAIFinal.html
# uses RELATIVE asset/nav paths (assets/..., offerings.html, ...), so this
# must be a real redirect (not a transparent rewrite) so the browser actually
# lands under /services/ and those relative paths resolve. Still a single
# edge-level 302 — no client JS round trip like the in-app /services route.
https://agentic.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai/services/*   /services/:splat         200
https://agentic.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai/*            /services/dsmAIFinal.html 302

# Creatives — creatives.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai falls through to the normal
# SPA fallback below (no rule needed here): App.tsx detects this hostname at
# runtime and renders the existing RegisteredCreatives page ("/creatives")
# as the "/" route for this host only, while every other route (/store,
# /cart, /account, ...) stays available via ordinary in-app client routing.

# Admin SPA (built from admin-app/ under /admin) — must come BEFORE the store fallback.
/admin/*              /admin/index.html                200

# Marketing & services microsites (standalone static pages, fast load).
/marketing            /marketing/index.html            302
/services             /services/dsmAIFinal.html        302

# SPA fallback for the React store / landing (every other client route).
/*                    /index.html                      200
